ab^2(a^4+b^8) &= a^5b^2+b^8 \\ &\ge 6\sqrt[6]{a^{20}b^{18}} \\ &= 6\sqrt[6]{(ab^2)^{20}} \\ &= 6 \times 5^{10/6} \\ &= 6 \times 5^{5/3}.
\end{align*}  The equality occurs when $a^5b^2 = b^8$, or equivalently, $a:b = 1:5$.  Therefore $a = {1\over 5^{5/6}}$ and $b = 5^{1/6}$, and the minimum value of $a^4+b^8$ is $6 \times 5^{5/3}.$ </think> <answer> $6 \times 5^{5/3}$ </answer>

